WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.339 --> 00:00:10.060
Last week was my birthday.

2
00:00:10.061 --> 00:00:17.030
My parents gave me a cool gift—my own smartphone.

3
00:00:17.030 --> 00:00:20.910
"Enjoying your new phone, Ella?" Dad asked.

4
00:00:20.910 --> 00:00:24.058
"Don't forget your online manners.

5
00:00:24.059 --> 00:00:28.303
"Number one: Think before you send or post."

6
00:00:28.303 --> 00:00:35.982
I groaned as Dad started listing our family's "netiquette rules."

7
00:00:35.982 --> 00:00:41.259
"Two: Never chat or share pictures with strangers . . ."

8
00:00:41.259 --> 00:00:44.868
By now I'd heard these rules a million times.

9
00:00:44.869 --> 00:00:49.230
While Dad continued reciting them, I looked down at my phone.

10
00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:52.875
I had a new message from my friend, Josh.

11
00:00:52.876 --> 00:00:56.250
Josh: Hey! Still want to go to the movies tomorrow?

12
00:00:56.250 --> 00:00:59.077
Ella: Yes!

13
00:00:59.078 --> 00:01:01.630
Josh: Great! Violet?

14
00:01:01.631 --> 00:01:05.531
I rolled my eyes.

15
00:01:05.531 --> 00:01:09.587
Josh, Violet, and I had been friends since third grade.

16
00:01:09.588 --> 00:01:13.094
But things started to change when we entered middle school.

17
00:01:13.095 --> 00:01:17.083
Violet had joined the drama club and made new friends.

18
00:01:17.084 --> 00:01:22.427
Now whenever she hung around with us, she sang songs from musicals—loudly.

19
00:01:22.427 --> 00:01:24.790
It got on my nerves.

20
00:01:24.790 --> 00:01:26.366
"Ella?"

21
00:01:26.366 --> 00:01:30.287
"Oops, sorry, Dad. Josh asked me something."

22
00:01:30.287 --> 00:01:32.493
He frowned.

23
00:01:32.494 --> 00:01:37.404
"Dad, you don't have to tell me about netiquette again," I said quickly.

24
00:01:37.405 --> 00:01:40.851
"Trust me—I know all the rules already."

25
00:01:40.851 --> 00:01:42.720
"Good." He nodded.

26
00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:49.302
"Then it's time to follow rule number five: no screen time until your chores are done."

27
00:01:49.302 --> 00:01:57.160
I saluted him. "Got it."

28
00:01:57.160 --> 00:02:02.413
Ella: No Violet tomorrow. I'm sick of her loud singing!

29
00:02:02.414 --> 00:02:08.622
I inserted an emoticon with a person plugging her ears, and then I went to fold laundry.

30
00:02:08.623 --> 00:02:12.993
The next day when I met Josh at the movie theater, he rushed up to me.

31
00:02:12.993 --> 00:02:16.949
"So, is Violet really angry?"

32
00:02:16.949 --> 00:02:20.115
"Angry about what?" I asked.

33
00:02:20.115 --> 00:02:22.687
"About what you said about her."

34
00:02:22.688 --> 00:02:25.479
"I don't know what you're talking about."

35
00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:27.780
Josh looked worried.

36
00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:32.247
"Yesterday when we were talking, it was a group chat."

37
00:02:32.247 --> 00:02:36.186
I blinked. "Does that mean . . .?"

38
00:02:36.186 --> 00:02:48.162
"Yep, Violet was in our chat too."

39
00:02:48.162 --> 00:02:53.383
Josh and I bought tickets and sat down.

40
00:02:53.383 --> 00:02:58.817
He started laughing at something on his phone, but I was too anxious to laugh at anything.

41
00:02:58.818 --> 00:03:02.501
I was thinking about how I'd insulted Violet.

42
00:03:02.501 --> 00:03:07.106
No Violet tomorrow. I'm sick of her loud singing!

43
00:03:07.106 --> 00:03:13.509
I felt terrible. Violet and I had grown apart, but she was still my friend.

44
00:03:13.509 --> 00:03:18.665
"Rule number one," I thought as tears slipped down my cheeks.

45
00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:22.336
"Think before you send."

46
00:03:22.336 --> 00:03:34.942
After the movie I biked over to Violet’s house.

47
00:03:34.943 --> 00:03:38.178
"I'm sorry, Violet," I blurted out.

48
00:03:38.179 --> 00:03:44.802
"I didn't realize it was a group chat and . . ." I kept talking, desperately trying to apologize.

49
00:03:44.802 --> 00:03:48.938
Violet looked away. "It's okay."

50
00:03:48.938 --> 00:03:53.316
I shook my head. "No, it's not."

51
00:03:53.317 --> 00:03:57.841
We stood in silence for a few moments, and then Violet looked up.

52
00:03:57.842 --> 00:04:01.300
"You definitely hurt my feelings, Ella.

53
00:04:01.301 --> 00:04:06.186
But my family says I do talk about theater stuff too much."

54
00:04:06.186 --> 00:04:09.104
She flashed a weak smile at me.

55
00:04:09.105 --> 00:04:14.216
"I'll try to stop singing show tunes, I promise."

56
00:04:14.216 --> 00:04:18.545
"I made such a stupid mistake," I mumbled.

57
00:04:18.545 --> 00:04:24.279
Violet nodded. "My parents always say to be cautious online.

58
00:04:24.280 --> 00:04:28.241
You can't take something back once you send it or post it."

59
00:04:28.241 --> 00:04:33.438
I swallowed. I'd learned that lesson the hard way.

60
00:04:33.438 --> 00:04:36.669
She shrugged and opened the door wider.

61
00:04:36.669 --> 00:04:39.508
"Want to come in for a while?"

62
00:04:39.508 --> 00:04:54.601
"Sure." I turned off my phone and then went inside.
